  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 2.2. Increased capacity of Member States to apply international labour standards</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The DWCP 2023-25 for South Sudan, aligned with the UN Sustainable Development Cooperation Framework (UNSDCF 2023-25), prioritizes an outcome on increased engagement in social dialogue and tripartism and an output that addressed issues raised by the  Committee of Experts on the Application of Conventions and Recommendations (CEACR) ILO supervisory bodies. This directly contribute to achieve the Outcome 1 of the UNSDCF 2023-2025 for South Sudan on  more transparent, accountable, and inclusive governance that enables the consolidation of peace, protects and promotes human rights. Furthermore,  the DWCP prioritizes Convention Nos. 081, 087, 122, 144 and 190 for ratification and domestication . With ILO technical inputs, South Sudan&apos;s United Nations Sustainable Development Cooperation (UNSDCF 2023-2025) was developed. Subsequently, with financial and technical support of ILO, the DWCP for South Sudan (2023-2025) was developed, including to address reporting challenges identified in the comments of the Committee of Experts on the Application of Conventions and Recommendations (CEACR). Priority 4, Output 4.1 focuses on the ratification and domestication of Conventions, as well as addressing reporting delays.</narrative>
   </description>
